        "### Relations: RiLM (arXiv:2609.10305) x All Previous Papers (standing rule)",
        "",
        "- **vs LayerMix (arXiv:2608.28930, s10-12): STACK (expected).** Flat-variant states stay Euclidean, so L2-LR/PLS probes apply unchanged - probe the geodesic model with the same heads. Hyp states would break probe geometry assumptions (non-Euclidean distances); probes on HypRiLM are untested by design.",
        "- **vs SABER (arXiv:2608.27963, s13): STACK (expected).** Confidence comes from the same softmax (geodesic logits feed Eq.4 math identically); CS/RSS arithmetic is decoder-agnostic. Untested combo, no shared state.",
        "- **vs Grokking (arXiv:2609.10657, s14/s16): THEME LINK, no code path shared.** Both are param-scarcity stories (Wout budget pressure ~= capacity pressure); grokking clocks could track a geodesic-head run (norm dynamics under tying are unmeasured - open experiment).",
        "- **vs ConvMem (arXiv:2609.10441, s15): NONE.** Different stages (readout geometry vs long-context scaffolding); no shared code path. Forced relations would be fake - recorded as none.",
        "- **vs Attention (arXiv:1706.03762) + BERT (arXiv:1810.04805, graded-only): NONE beyond backbone.** GeodesicHead replaces the readout of whatever backbone path is live, including Attn:: variants (composition by design).",
