      "source": [
        "### Backprop: TASCO (arXiv:2609.11393, s21) x later papers up to 2609.04463 (additive back-links; no prior line touched)\n",
        "\n",
        "- **Paper 11 is the direct mechanism test of TASCO's transfer claim:** loadings on verbal items under RP/SAP prefixes - does stability-aware adaptation re-engage the numeric circuit, or merely sharpen the wrong one? Confidence-only steering cannot distinguish these; loading can.\n",
        "- **Entropy is TASCO's objective AND paper 11 App D's strongest control, while loading carries unique variance in all three formats** - the paper already proves complementarity, so TASCO should monitor loading alongside entropy instead of optimizing blind to it.\n",
        "- **Prefix-steered states still carry loadings** (stack on the same forward pass); a loading-term TASCO variant (steer toward the circuit, not just low entropy) is the intractable-looking next step - AP gradients per optimization step are prohibitive, but a frozen S_m probe is a cheap surrogate objective.\n",
        "- **How TASCO fares into future dev:** it graduates from accuracy-only eval to mechanism-checked adaptation the moment the s23 pipeline runs on its prefixes - the eval harness already exists.\n",
