    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 22. Direction of Ignorance \u2013 The Geometry of Ignorance: LLMs Know When to Temper Bayesian Priors (Liu et al. 2026, arXiv:2609.02959; no public code found)",
        "",
        "**Paper in one paragraph.** One unembedding direction encodes the corpus unigram: softmax(W d)=p_uni (Eq.1), found by centered OLS of log-freqs on unembedding rows (Eq.4/9, unique by normal equations, no forward passes). Final states split y=lam*d+y_ctx (Eq.2); lam=dhat'y/beta (Eq.5) is the tempered-Bayes exponent p~p_uni^lam*L_ctx (Eq.7: <0 invert, 0 remove, (0,1) soften, 1 Bayes, >1 sharpen). Universal across 4 families (Table 1: R2 .75-.92, nKL<=0.083); learned not innate (Fig.2); declines with coherent (not long/shuffled) context (Fig.3 + A/B switch); causal under Eq.8 patching with random-direction control flat (Fig.4, lam0=0.46+-0.20); |lam| falls with dim (Fig.5, Gemma-1B exception); distributed population code, not a neuron (Fig.10/G: neurons write INTO d_prior).",
        "",
        "**Repo note:** no public code anywhere (0 issues reviewable) - text-faithful. Integration reasoning (s17 rule): fit + readout + intervention are readout-side analyses on live weights (lm_head) and final states (hooks). No architecture change, so plain orchestrator cells, no new Techniques. Adaptations with consequences: corpus = Shakespeare training text (not Pile - documents the corpus-dependence limit, s7); coverage c=1.0 (65-char vocab fully observed; paper c=0.7 exists for BPE tails we don't have); under GeodesicHead there is no Wout, so fit on the shared token_embedding table instead (documented below).",
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# ALWAYS-PRESENT ignorance-direction fit | Paper Eq.4/9 (centered OLS, unique), Eq.11 (R2), s3.3 (nKL), App B (streaming/c=0.7), App C Table 1 | graded 10_Equations/10_Table1_Fits | plain codeblock, no Impl tag by design.\n",
        "\"\"\"Recover d_prior from the live readout matrix + corpus counts (no forward passes).\"\"\"\n",
        "\"\"\"W = lm_head.weight normally; under GeodesicHead (no Wout) the shared token table \"\"\"\n",
        "\"\"\"serves as W (documented analog: tying makes input and output geometry coincide).\"\"\"\n",
        "\"\"\"Counts come from the training text (corpus-dependence limit, s7). c=1.0: tiny vocab.\"\"\"\n",
        "def ignorance_fit_dprior(model, counts):\n",
        "    import torch as _t\n",
        "    import numpy as _np\n",
        "    W = model.lm_head.weight.detach().double() if hasattr(model.lm_head, \"weight\") else model.token_embedding.weight.detach().double()\n",
        "    n = _np.array([counts.get(i, 0) for i in range(W.shape[0])], dtype=float)\n",
        "    n = n[n > 0]\n",
        "    Wf = W[:len(n)]\n",
        "    p = n / n.sum()\n",
        "    ell = _np.log(p)\n",
        "    Wc = Wf.numpy() - Wf.numpy().mean(0, keepdims=True)\n",
        "    lc = ell - ell.mean()\n",
        "    d, *_ = _np.linalg.lstsq(Wc, lc, rcond=None)\n",
        "    beta = float(_np.linalg.norm(d))\n",
        "    dhat = d / max(beta, 1e-12)\n",
        "    r = lc - Wc @ d\n",
        "    orth = bool(abs(float((Wc.T @ r).max())) < 1e-6)\n",
        "    r2 = 1 - float(r @ r) / max(float(lc @ lc), 1e-12)\n",
        "    import numpy as _nq\n",
        "    z = Wf.numpy() @ (beta * dhat)\n",
        "    z = z - z.max()\n",
        "    pp = _nq.exp(z) / _nq.exp(z).sum()\n",
        "    uni = _nq.full(len(p), 1 / len(p))\n",
        "    kl = lambda a, b: float((a * (_nq.log(a) - _nq.log(b))).sum())\n",
        "    nkl = kl(p, pp) / max(kl(p, uni), 1e-12)\n",
        "    return {\"dhat\": dhat, \"beta\": beta, \"r2\": r2, \"orth\": orth, \"nkl\": nkl}\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# ALWAYS-PRESENT prior-loading tracker + controls | Paper Eq.5 (lam), Eq.6-7 (logit split, tempered Bayes), s4/Fig.3 (decay, 70B-negative, shuffled flat, A/B switch), App E Fig.7 | graded 10_Fig3_Dynamics | plain codeblock, no Impl tag by design.\n",
        "\"\"\"Per-position lam over passages; coherent-vs-shuffled and A/B-switch controls.\"\"\"\n",
        "\"\"\"y = final pre-unembedding state (ln_final output at last position, Eq.2 site).\"\"\"\n",
        "\"\"\"Tempering readout: lam<0 invert / 0 remove / (0,1) soften / 1 Bayes / >1 sharpen.\"\"\"\n",
        "def ignorance_lambda_track(model, dhat, beta, passages):\n",
        "    import torch as _t\n",
        "    dev = next(model.parameters()).device\n",
        "    lam_curves = []\n",
        "    for ids in passages:\n",
        "        xb = _t.tensor([ids], dtype=_t.long).to(dev)\n",
        "        curve = []\n",
        "        with _t.no_grad():\n",
        "            for t in range(1, len(ids) + 1):\n",
        "                pos = _t.arange(t, device=dev).unsqueeze(0)\n",
        "                emb = model.token_embedding(xb[:, :t]) + model.position_embedding(pos)\n",
        "                h = model.blocks(emb)\n",
        "                y = model.ln_final(h)[:, -1, :].float().cpu().numpy()\n",
        "                curve.append(float(y @ dhat) / max(beta, 1e-12))\n",
        "        lam_curves.append(curve)\n",
        "    return lam_curves\n",
        "\n",
        "def ignorance_controls(model, dhat, beta, passages, seed=0):\n",
        "    import random as _r\n",
        "    r = _r.Random(seed)\n",
        "    out = {\"coherent\": ignorance_lambda_track(model, dhat, beta, passages)}\n",
        "    out[\"shuffled\"] = ignorance_lambda_track(model, dhat, beta, [sorted(p, key=lambda _: r.random()) for p in passages])\n",
        "    if len(passages) >= 2:\n",
        "        cut = len(passages[0]) // 2\n",
        "        spliced = [passages[0][:cut] + passages[1][cut:cut + cut]]\n",
        "        out[\"ab_switch\"] = ignorance_lambda_track(model, dhat, beta, spliced)\n",
        "    return out\n",
        "\n",
        "def ignorance_tempering_zone(lam):\n",
        "    if lam < 0:\n",
        "        return \"invert\"\n",
        "    if lam == 0:\n",
        "        return \"remove\"\n",
        "    if lam < 1:\n",
        "        return \"soften\"\n",
        "    if lam == 1:\n",
        "        return \"bayes\"\n",
        "    return \"sharpen\"\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# ALWAYS-PRESENT lambda intervention | Paper Eq.8 (y(lam*) patch), Fig.4 (KL monotonic, random flat, lam0=0.46+-0.20), s5/App G (causal, distributed) | graded 10_Fig4_Intervention | plain codeblock, no Impl tag by design.\n",
        "\"\"\"Patch final-state loading to lam* (others fixed), measure KL to unigram prior.\"\"\"\n",
        "\"\"\"Control: magnitude-matched random-direction patch must leave KL flat. Under \"\"\"\n",
        "\"\"\"GeodesicHead there is no W: patch the shared table direction instead (documented).\"\"\"\n",
        "def ignorance_intervene(model, dhat, beta, y, lam_star, punigram, seed=0):\n",
        "    import torch as _t\n",
        "    import numpy as _nq\n",
        "    lam0 = float(y @ dhat) / max(beta, 1e-12)\n",
        "    d = beta * _t.tensor(dhat, dtype=y.dtype)\n",
        "    yp = y + (lam_star - lam0) * d\n",
        "    W = model.lm_head.weight.detach() if hasattr(model.lm_head, \"weight\") else model.token_embedding.weight.detach()\n",
        "    lp = _t.softmax(W.double() @ yp.double(), dim=0).numpy()\n",
        "    pu = _nq.array(punigram, dtype=float)\n",
        "    kl = float((lp * (_nq.log(lp.clip(min=1e-12)) - _nq.log(pu.clip(min=1e-12)))).sum())\n",
        "    g = _t.Generator().manual_seed(seed)\n",
        "    rnd = _t.randn(y.shape[0], generator=g, dtype=y.dtype)\n",
        "    rnd = rnd / rnd.norm().clamp_min(1e-12) * d.norm()\n",
        "    yr = y + (lam_star - lam0) * rnd\n",
        "    lr = _t.softmax(W.double() @ yr.double(), dim=0).numpy()\n",
        "    klr = float((lr * (_nq.log(lr.clip(min=1e-12)) - _nq.log(pu.clip(min=1e-12)))).sum())\n",
        "    return {\"lam0\": lam0, \"kl_prior\": kl, \"kl_random\": klr}\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### Compatibility: The Geometry of Ignorance (Liu et al. 2026, arXiv:2609.02959)",
        "",
        "- **STACK:** fit + tracker + intervention read live weights/states only (zero training); lam augments LayerMix probe heads as a hallucination feature (paper s6 proposes exactly this - untested stack, highest-value open combo in the file); tracker + checkpoint probing (lam curve over training = training diagnostic, s6); shuffled/A-B controls + Corrupt eval sets (same control logic).",
        "- **ALTERNATIVE (pick 1):** corpus for counts (Shakespeare-training-text now; Pile-scale later - changes d_prior, document which); W source under linear head (lm_head.weight) vs geodesic head (shared token table); coherent | shuffled | A-B per measurement run.",
        "- **NEVER-SAME-PATH:** d_prior fit on one corpus read as another corpus's prior (corpus-dependence limit, s7); lam values compared across different beta normalizations (always divide by the fit's own beta, Eq.5); intervention claims without the random-direction control (flat-control required, Fig.4).",
        "",
        "### Relations: Ignorance (arXiv:2609.02959) x All Previous Papers (standing rule)",
        "",
        "- **vs LayerMix (arXiv:2608.28930, s10-12): STACK (expected, high value).** Paper s6 explicitly proposes lam-driven hallucination detectors; lam is a scalar probe feature computable per token from frozen states - appends to any probe head without touching probe math. Untested combo, flagged as priority.",
        "- **vs RiLM (arXiv:2609.10305, s19): SHARED OBJECT, documented fork.** d_prior lives in the unembedding W; GeodesicHead deletes Wout, so under geodesicflat the fit runs on the shared token table instead (same OLS math, different matrix). Linear-head and geodesic-head lam values are NOT comparable (different geometries) - methodological ban.",
        "- **vs SABER (arXiv:2608.27963, s13): STACK (expected).** Prior loading (what the model falls back on) complements confidence stability (how steadily it predicts): high-lam + high-CS = confident ignorance, the precise failure mode both papers circle. Untested combo.",
        "- **vs TASCO (arXiv:2609.11393, s21): STACK (expected).** Prefix-steered states still carry lam; variance diagnostics and lam curves observe the same runs from complementary angles (stability of confidence vs loading of prior).",
        "- **vs Grokking (arXiv:2609.10657, s14/s16): STACK (expected).** Paper s6 proposes tracking lam over training as a regime-shift diagnostic (unigram-matching to context-driven); grokking clocks + norm tracker are the natural host loop. Untested combo.",
        "- **vs ConvMem (arXiv:2609.10441, s15): NONE.** Readout geometry vs long-context scaffolding; no shared code path.",
        "- **vs WRP (arXiv:2609.09883, s20): STACK (expected).** Fit + tracker re-run on pruned checkpoints: does the prior direction survive block removal (training-diagnostic use, s6)? Untested combo.",
        "- **vs Attention (arXiv:1706.03762) + BERT (arXiv:1810.04805, graded-only): NONE.** Reads whatever backbone path is live.",
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
